US-008 is done. Summary of what was implemented:

**Routes (authorization now declared on the route)**
- `backend/src/api/project/routes/project.js` — `createCoreRouter` with `is-authenticated` on `find`/`findOne`, plus `has-permission` `CREATE_PROJECT` / `UPDATE_PROJECT` / `DELETE_PROJECT` on `create`/`update`/`delete` (codes read from the controller before changing it). No `auth: false` on core routes, per the US-007 learning.
- `backend/src/api/project/routes/01-custom-project.js` — `PUT /projects/:id/change-status` now `auth: false` + `is-authenticated` + `has-permission CHANGE_PROJECT_STATUS` (it was previously `auth: false` with nothing else, relying solely on the handler).
- `backend/src/api/comment/routes/comment.js` — `is-authenticated` on all five actions; `create` additionally requires `COMMENT_DOCUMENT`. `update`/`delete` intentionally only require a session.

**Controllers**
- `project.js` — dropped the `protectedController` import and every `authenticate()`/`authorize()` call; each handler uses `const user = ctx.state.user;` and keeps the ownership checks (`isElevated`/`applyFilter`/`requireProjectAccess`) and audit logging.
- `comment.js` — same, except `canModifyComment` still imports and calls `authorize(..., 'MANAGE_COMMENTS', ...)` for the moderation path. `create` still overwrites `correctionTutor` with `ctx.state.user.id` and `update` still strips it from the body.

**Tests** — the 8 existing project/comment tests are unchanged; 14 new HTTP cases verify the policies are wired (no token, missing permission on core and custom routes, success with audit `userId` from `ctx.state.user`, body-supplied `correctionTutor` ignored, author can edit without `MANAGE_COMMENTS`, stranger gets 403, moderator can delete). `cd backend && npm test`: **52/52 passing**.

`backend/package.json` is untouched. Learnings and a new Codebase Pattern (record-dependent permissions stay in the controller) are appended to `.ralph-tui/progress.md`. No commits were made.

